                  %mi IIB
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi S
                  %mi IIB
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  IIB \overset{S}{\leftrightarrow} IIB
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HoaravaWittenCompactifications.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics taken from
              %a{:href => "#HoravaWitten95"} Horava-Witten 95, p. 15
          %p
            If one considers this situation additionally with a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            quotient of the first circle factor, one obtains the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and heterotic string theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"}> Horava-Witten theory
            ). If instead one performs it on the second circle factor, one obtains
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"} type I string theory
          %p
            Here in both cases the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            is by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection"} reflection
            of the circle at a line through its center. Hence if we identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \simeq \mathbb{R} / \mathbb{Z}
            then the action is by multiplication by /1 on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
          %p In summary:
          %p M-theory on
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⫽
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mi B
                        %mn 1
