                yields
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi S
                          %mi B
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⫽
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times \left( S^1_B \sslash \mathbb{Z}_2 \right)
                yields
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I%27+string+theory"} type I' string theory
          %p
            Hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            that swaps the two circle factors corresponds to a duality between heterotic E and type I’ string theory. And T-dualizing turns this into a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+type+I+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between type I and heterotic string theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi HE
                        %mtd
                          %mover
