                    theories in six dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.0711"} arXiv:1404.0711
            %li
              %p
                Kantaro Ohmori, Hiroyuki Shimizu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mi T
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1/T^2
                    Compactifications of 6d
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = (1,0)
                    Theories and Brane Webs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.03195"} arXiv:1509.03195
            %li#HKLY15
              %p
                Hirotaka Hayashi, Sung-Soo Kim, Kimyeong Lee, Futoshi Yagi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 6d SCFTs, 5d Dualities and Tao Web Diagrams
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.03300"} arXiv:1509.03300
            %li
              %p
                Ibrahima Bah, Achilleas Passias,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Tomasiello"} Alessandro Tomasiello
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi AdS
                            %mn 5
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5
                    compactifications with punctures in massive IIA supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.07389"} arXiv:1704.07389
          %h3#ReferencesSugimotoStringTheory Sugimoto string theory
          %p
            What is now called
            %em Sugimoto string theory
            is a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            version of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"} type I string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            on an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %msup
                    %mn 9
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O9^+
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            (instead of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %msup
                      %mn 9
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O9^-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field+tadpole+cancellation"} RR-field tadpole cancellation
            by 32
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-brane"} anti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D9-branes"} D9-branes
            (instead of plain D9-branes), whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi USp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 32
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} USp(32)
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Sugimoto99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"}> Shigeki Sugimoto
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Anomaly Cancellations in the Type I D9-anti-D9 System and the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi USp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 32
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} USp(32)
                  String Theory
              %strong 102
              (1999) 685-699 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9905159"}> arXiv:hep-th/9905159
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1143/PTP.102.685"} doi:10.1143/PTP.102.685
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Sanefumi Moriyama:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi USp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 32
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} USp(32)
                    String as Spontaneously Supersymmetry Broken Theory
                %strong 522
                (2001) 177-180 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0107203"}> arXiv:hep-th/0107203
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(01)01278-3"} doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(01)01278-3
            %li
              %p
                Hector Parra de Freitas, p. 166 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Compactifications with Half-maximal Supersymmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://theses.hal.science/tel-04234221"} hal/tel-04234221
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://theses.hal.science/tel-04234221v1/file/133300_PARRA_DE_FREITAS_2023_archivage.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Vittorio Larotonda, Ling Lin:
                %em Anomaly Inflow and Gauge Group Topology in the 10d Sugimoto String Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.17894"}> arXiv:2412.17894
                \&amp;rbrack;
